{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725","id":5534896146,"node_id":"I_kwDON109P88AAAABSefQEg","number":1725,"title":"Authenticated Google Meet bots launch Chromium with --incognito and ignore restored session","user":{"login":"cipher-gb","id":283700096,"node_id":"U_kgDOEOjrgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/283700096?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb","html_url":"https://github.com/cipher-gb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cipher-gb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-09-22T03:20:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T12:54:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nAuthenticated Google Meet bots restore their persistent browser profile, but the browser is then launched with `--incognito`. Chromium does not use the restored profile cookies for the incognito context, so the bot reaches Meet as a signed-out guest and fails the authenticated-session check.\n\n## Affected code\n\nThis is present in v0.13.1 and in the current `vexaai/vexa-bot:v012` image:\n\n- `JOIN_BROWSER_ARGS` contains `--incognito`: https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/blob/v0.13.1/core/meetings/modules/join/src/browser-args.ts#L43-L45\n- `launchBrowser()` unconditionally combines those args with `getAuthenticatedBrowserArgs()`: https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/blob/v0.13.1/core/meetings/services/bot/src/capture-bridge.ts#L592-L596\n\n```ts\nconst args = [...getAuthenticatedBrowserArgs(), ...getJoinBrowserArgs()];\n```\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Provision a signed-in Google browser profile and upload it to the configured userdata S3 path.\n2. Start a Google Meet bot with `authenticated: true` and that userdata path.\n3. The profile restore succeeds, but Meet renders the guest name field instead of the signed-in account.\n4. The bot exits with `auth_session_missing`.\n\nRemoving `--incognito` from the authenticated launch makes Chromium use the restored profile. Guest bots should retain the flag.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nAuthenticated launches should exclude `--incognito`; anonymous/guest launches should keep the existing canonical join args.\n\nOne possible localized fix is:\n\n```ts\nconst joinArgs = getJoinBrowserArgs();\nconst args = [\n  ...getAuthenticatedBrowserArgs(),\n  ...(inv.authenticated\n    ? joinArgs.filter((arg) => arg !== \"--incognito\")\n    : joinArgs),\n];\n```\n\nA regression test should cover both branches so the guest isolation behavior is preserved.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1725/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}